{"verdicts":[{"coverage":{"complete":true,"interactions":["gate.execute (execution.js:1000) and review.execute (boundary-review.js:311) both call checkClaims before any reviewer starts or any result is recorded; review.execute also passes the claims on to gate.execute","Retained claims (after claim-not-retained drops) feed packetSweepRecords, then value.sweepRecords and the packet; the input identity is part of the reuse check","Earlier review inputs are matched on roundPolicy scope, epoch and revision, then read by scopeSweepRecords at packet time and at pair qualification (boundaryReviews, then roundSchedule, then scheduledBlocking)","The prepass in review-findings.js uses the round key (scope, epoch, round, revision) and per-provider perspectives, and interacts with origin and resolved tracking and with the trail-based history selection in execution.js","The roundPolicy epoch comes from reviewScopeHistory closures (amendment, split, integration) in round-policy.js","Instruction-text changes interact with the reviewContract fingerprint and the unchanged REVIEW_CONTRACT_VERSION when retained results are reused","The desktop mirror copies, desktop-projection.json and workflow-inventory.json are checked by the desktop tests and the portability lint"],"limitations":[],"paths":["repository/plugin-src/shared/resources/protocol/current/sweep-records.js","repository/apps/desktop/resources/protocol/current/sweep-records.js","repository/plugin-src/shared/resources/protocol/current/execution.js","repository/apps/desktop/resources/protocol/current/execution.js","repository/plugin-src/shared/resources/protocol/current/boundary-review.js","repository/apps/desktop/resources/protocol/current/boundary-review.js","repository/plugin-src/shared/resources/protocol/current/review-findings.js","repository/apps/desktop/resources/protocol/current/review-findings.js","repository/plugin-src/shared/resources/protocol/current/round-policy.js","repository/apps/desktop/resources/protocol/current/round-policy.js","repository/plugin-src/shared/resources/PROTOCOL.md","repository/plugin-src/shared/resources/commands/pr-review.md","repository/plugin-src/contracts/workflow-inventory.json","repository/apps/desktop/resources/desktop-projection.json","repository/cli/src/commands/current.js","repository/cli/test/sweep-records.test.js","repository/cli/test/helpers/sweep-fixture.js","repository/cli/test/round-policy.test.js","repository/cli/test/current-boundary-review.test.js","repository/cli/test/current-core.test.js"]},"coverageDecisions":[],"criteria":[{"evidence":"Unit tests in sweep-records.test.js:19-28 cover: a missing disposition and an unknown one ('resolved'), with the refusal naming claims[i].disposition; a fixed claim without a sweep and a disputed claim with one, naming claims[i].sweep; an unknown key ('note'); an empty claim; more than 128 claims; and an accepted disputed claim.\n\nThe entry-point test (lines 91-107) shows refusals through review.execute (missing disposition; disputed with a sweep) and through gate.execute (fixed without a sweep; missing sweep.search). It checks that launches() === 0 and that state.results.length is unchanged, and that a valid disputed claim through review.execute launches reviewers. Both entry points call the same checkClaims as their first validation step (execution.js:1000, boundary-review.js:311). The receipt passes.","id":"R1","outcome":"PASS"},{"evidence":"sweep-records.test.js:30-48 checks:\n- each of the six fields refused by path when missing;\n- each text field refused when empty, whitespace-only, 42, null, an array, or 4097 characters, with 4096 accepted;\n- sites refused when it is a string, an object, an empty list, or 257 entries;\n- sites[1] refused when it is not an object, has an unknown key ('column'), has a path that is missing, empty, numeric or 1025 characters, or has a line of undefined, 0, -1, 1.5 or '3';\n- an unknown sweep key ('owner') and a non-object sweep refused;\n- a one-site record and a 256-site record accepted.\nThe receipt passes.","id":"R2","outcome":"PASS"},{"evidence":"sweep-records.test.js:109-162 checks:\n- the round-4 paired packets carry exactly [{findingId F0, classId 'swept-class', round 4, the sweep fields}], plus format, guide, roundPolicy.revision (sha256) and epoch 0;\n- round 5 without claims carries the same single record, even though both peers' inputs held it;\n- an individual tagged review in round 6 receives that record plus its own re-claim as a second record (round 6);\n- with reviewScopes empty, or a closure added to reviewScopeHistory (a new epoch), scopeSweepRecords returns [];\n- a stale fixed claim is dropped, leaving no sweepRecords field and claims [], with roundPolicy.revision present;\n- uniqueRecords removes records with equal content.\nThe receipt passes.","id":"R3","outcome":"PASS"},{"evidence":"sweep-records.test.js:164-187 runs for rounds 4 and 5. The revision changes app.js only and the findings are on app/other.js, so the path-based regression rule cannot apply. Results: a new medium swept-class finding gives FAIL; an earlier F1 of the class marked present gives FAIL; an other-class medium finding gives PASS with one demoted finding; the claimed F0 still present gives PASS. The predicate unit test (lines 189-197) covers another ID, the own ID, another class, a later round, a null round and a missing classId. The receipt passes all eight round tests and the predicate test.","id":"R4","outcome":"PASS"},{"evidence":"execution.js:289 contains 'When packet.sweepRecords is present, follow packet.sweepRecords.guide.' and line 290 adds 'missed sites of a class in packet.sweepRecords' to the rounds 4-5 band. SWEEP_GUIDE (sweep-records.js:23) tells reviewers to verify each record's search, sites, fix, test and dependents; to report a missed site with the record's classId; and that such a finding is a regression of the previous fix where a medium or high one blocks in rounds 4-5. sweep-records.test.js:199-206 asserts this text, and the receipt passes.","id":"R5","outcome":"PASS"},{"evidence":"round-policy.test.js:569-613 runs five #134 variants: codex re-reports and claude resolves; claude re-reports and codex resolves; unsupported instead of resolved; and two individual tagged reviews in each order, which also asserts status round 4. Each asserts that round 5 is FAIL. Additional same-revision cases are at lines 618-715. The receipt shows all 42 round-policy tests passing, including every pre-existing one. The low-severity CR8-1 edge case does not affect any stated R6 scenario.","id":"R6","outcome":"PASS"},{"evidence":"PROTOCOL.md:357-377 adds the swept-class regression rule, the re-report rule, per-provider perspectives and the scope epoch to the round policy. PROTOCOL.md:735-769, 'Fix claims and sweep records', covers dispositions, the six sweep fields and their limits, refusals before launch, the packet field and its records, de-duplication, closed scopes and the regression rule. commands/pr-review.md:23-31 explains how to write fixed and disputed claims and the sweep. Receipt 5 (`diff -r plugin-src/shared/resources/protocol apps/desktop/resources/protocol`) exited 0 with empty output, so the mirror is byte-identical.","id":"R7","outcome":"PASS"}],"dimensions":[{"evidence":"New module (current/sweep-records.js):\n- checkClaims (lines 51-66) enforces exactly findingId, claim, disposition and sweep; disposition must be fixed or disputed; fixed needs a sweep and disputed must not carry one.\n- checkSweep (33-47) enforces the six required fields, a 4096-character limit on text, 1 to 256 sites, and site paths of at most 1024 characters with positive integer lines. Every refusal names its field path.\n- claimRecords (76-81) takes classId from the first retained report and round from roundPolicy.\n- scopeSweepRecords (87-103) only reads review inputs whose roundPolicy scope and epoch match and whose revision is in the open scope, so closed scopes contribute nothing.\n- sweptClassRegression (116-119) skips null-round records, later rounds and the record's own findingId.\n\nWiring:\n- boundary-review.js:42-47 ORs the swept-class regression into scheduledBlocking only when round >= 4. It never changes a reviewer's blocking flag, and round-policy.js:104-110 still returns false for non-blocking or low findings.\n- execution.js:1168 adds epoch and revision to roundPolicy. Line 1170 builds the records after dropped claims are filtered out. Lines 1205 and 1287 add the records to the reuse check and the packet.\n- execution.js:1039-1049 replaces the old single `reopened` slot with a per-finding trail; history selection and prioritisation both read it.\n- review-findings.js:43-67 implements the round key, the latest report per provider and the rule that re-reports count as present.\n\nThe evaluator instructions match the base text plus two additions: lines 289-290 add the packet.sweepRecords.guide sentence and the band clause about missed sites. Because REVIEW_CONTRACT_VERSION is unchanged and reviewContract fingerprints the instructions (line 313), a retained result written under the old text cannot qualify.\n\nOne low defect: CR8-1. There are no high or medium defects.","name":"code","outcome":"PASS"},{"evidence":"AC1 and AC2 are enforced by checkClaims and its tests (sweep-records.test.js:19-48, 91-107).\n\nAC3:\n- Records with classId and round reach the paired round, the next round and an individual tagged review.\n- A re-claim of the same finding is kept as a second record; a dropped claim adds nothing; without records the packet has no sweepRecords field.\n- Closed scopes and later epochs carry no records, and roundPolicy.revision is present (tests at lines 109-162).\n\nAC4: rounds 4 and 5 are covered for a new swept-class finding (FAIL), a still-present earlier finding (FAIL), another class (demoted to PASS) and the claimed finding itself (PASS); the predicate has unit tests (lines 164-197).\n\nAC5: the guide text and the instruction sentence are tested (lines 199-206).\n\nAC6: five #134 variants plus same-revision re-review cases are in round-policy.test.js:569-715.\n\nAC7: PROTOCOL.md covers the round policy (lines 357-377) and 'Fix claims and sweep records' (lines 735-769); pr-review.md:23-31 explains how to write claims; the mirror diff receipt shows the copies are identical.\n\nDecision reconciliation:\n- The code matches S5-S7, S10, S11, S14 and S15 (DEC-2 to DEC-5). Examples: S7 two-claim class regression (sweptClassRegression compares findingId); S10 scope epoch; S11 per-provider latest perspective; S15 trail.\n- S16 keeps main's REVIEW_CONTRACT_VERSION, which is safe because of the fingerprint check.\n- Project rule: new protocol modules must be listed in workflow-inventory.json and desktop-projection.json; both list current/sweep-records.js (inventory line 294, projection line 209).","name":"requirements","outcome":"PASS"},{"evidence":"All 11 receipts in the consumed Verification ran on 94d1183 with exit code 0.\n- Focused run of sweep-records and round-policy: 58 of 58 tests pass. Stdout lists every R1-R6 test, including all five #134 variants.\n- Affected suites: 7 files (boundary-review, core, reviewer-contract, verdict-normalization, history-assessment, ci-after-convergence, autonomous); 12 other drivers of gate.execute and review.execute; and self-validation plus review-packet.\n- Also: plugin validate, lint and validate-native; the portability lint (declared inventory, the gap that failed hosted CI in S12); the protocol mirror diff; `npm test` for apps/desktop; and the --claims help-text grep.\n\nI checked every cli/test file that calls gate.execute, review.execute, boundaryReviews, executeGates or findingObligations: all 20 are covered by these receipts.\n\nGap (EV8-1, low): current-cli.test.js and gatereeve-cli.test.js exercise cli/src/commands/current.js, which changed one option description, and have no local receipt. The help-grep receipt checks the changed text directly.\n\nThe implementer's proposed local alternative is adequate for local rounds. ciRequiredChecks lists 'Ubuntu 22.04 acceptance', 'Ubuntu 24.04 acceptance' and 'Desktop contract on Ubuntu 24.04'. In plugin-ci.yml the acceptance jobs run ci/portable-acceptance.sh: the full `npm test --prefix cli` (including the host-dependent files and both CLI files above), plugin validate, validate-native, lint and build. The desktop contract job runs `npm run check`. That plan covers the approved scope. No hosted CI has run on this head yet; that is the post-convergence step and is not recorded here as a success.","name":"evidence","outcome":"PASS"},{"evidence":"The changes are limited to the planned P1-P7 areas: the sweep-records.js module and its desktop mirror; edits to execution.js, boundary-review.js, review-findings.js and round-policy.js (scopeEpoch) and their mirrors; PROTOCOL.md and commands/pr-review.md; workflow-inventory.json and desktop-projection.json; the --claims help text in cli/src/commands/current.js; and the new or updated tests. The base already includes main's #171 work (for example afterMergeCriteria is present in base execution.js), so the planning and core paths in regressionPaths are not part of this feature diff. The only caller-visible contract change, that claims now need a disposition, is documented. No non-test callers that build claims in the old shape remain: I searched plugin-src, apps/desktop and cli/src.","name":"scope","outcome":"PASS"},{"evidence":"There were no earlier findings needing a disposition (dispositionsRequired is empty), and historyGaps meant a fresh full assessment.\n\nNew findings:\n- CR8-1 (low, R6): in the #134 prepass, a later same-round report from the same provider that makes no assessment replaces that provider's re-report.\n- EV8-1 (low, gate:review): no local receipts for the CLI test files that exercise the changed current.js.\n\nBoth are low and non-blocking. In the hand-back band only high findings and medium regressions of the previous fix block, and neither finding is either.","name":"findings","outcome":"PASS"}],"dispositions":[],"findings":[{"blocking":false,"classId":"round-perspective-superseded-by-no-assessment","classStatement":"A same-provider, same-round report that makes no assessment (UNAVAILABLE or empty) replaces that provider's earlier present or re-report perspective in the peer prepass","criterion":"R6","evidence":"review-findings.js:55-62 builds `present` only from dispositions and re-reports, then sets `perspectives.set(provider, present)` for every history report whatever its outcome, so a later report with no findings or dispositions replaces an earlier one. In execution.js:1020-1028, latestContext keeps the latest review report for each gate and criterion with no outcome filter, so an UNAVAILABLE same-round report can enter the next round's history. The planning path has an equivalent guard, tested by 'a completed UNAVAILABLE planning review never clears a regression'; no boundary test covers this case. It needs an unusual combination (peer disagreement, a later same-revision execution, a provider failure, and that failure being the latest result), so it is low and non-blocking in the hand-back band.","failureScenario":"A medium regression F is raised in round 3. In round 4 codex re-reports F and claude-code marks it resolved. Later in round 4, a same-revision codex execution (an individual tagged review or a second review.execute) comes back UNAVAILABLE and is recorded last, so execution.js latestContext picks it up as round-5 history. Its empty perspective replaces codex's re-report at review-findings.js:60-62, so peerPresent is false and claude's resolved clears F's origin. In round 5 codex's FAIL on F is judged afresh, demoted, and the pair is reported as PASS.","id":"CR8-1","path":"repository/plugin-src/shared/resources/protocol/current/review-findings.js","severity":"low"},{"blocking":false,"classId":"missing-affected-suite-receipt","classStatement":"A changed source file's CLI test suites have no local Verification receipt on the candidate tree","criterion":"gate:review","evidence":"current.js:175 changes only the option description string (base: 'JSON list of findingId and implementer claim pairs'). None of the 11 receipts in evidence/f5d3582d… lists cli/test/current-cli.test.js or cli/test/gatereeve-cli.test.js. Receipt 7 greps the new help text and passed, gatereeve-cli.test.js:43-44 only checks /actual receipts/ and /run-eligible/, and ci/portable-acceptance.sh:21 runs the full CLI suite in the planned required CI jobs, so the risk is low.","failureScenario":"The --claims option description in cli/src/commands/current.js changes, but current-cli.test.js (`evaluate verification` through the CLI) and gatereeve-cli.test.js (`evaluate --help`) were not run locally. A CLI-level regression in that command module would only show up in hosted CI after convergence.","id":"EV8-1","path":"repository/cli/src/commands/current.js","severity":"low"}],"gate":"review","historyAssessment":null,"mandateAssessment":null,"outcome":"PASS","summary":"Round 8 (hand-back band) fresh full review of FEATURE tb-convergence-sweep-records at head 94d1183 against base and target a6f2e8a. The base and target are the same commit, and the base already contains main's #142 and #171 work. So the feature diff is just the sweep-record and #134 change; the other regressionPaths entries (planning*.js, core.js, delegation.js and so on) come from the main merge and are already in the base. I did a fresh assessment because historyGaps is nonempty; dispositionsRequired is empty.\n\nWhat the code does:\n- One function, checkClaims, validates every claim's disposition and sweep record. Both entry points call it before anything else (execution.js:1000 and boundary-review.js:311).\n- Packets carry the open scope's records, matched on scope, epoch and revision (packetSweepRecords and scopeSweepRecords).\n- When a pair is qualified, roundSchedule.blocks treats sweptClassRegression as a regression.\n- For #134, the review-findings.js prepass groups reports by scope, epoch, round and revision; each provider's latest report is its perspective, and a re-report counts as present.\n- In execution.js, each finding keeps a history trail, so it keeps the review that raised it and every later report that reopened or closed it.\n\nThe tests and docs meet R1 through R7. All 11 local receipts ran on this tree and passed. I raised two low, non-blocking findings:\n- CR8-1: a later same-round report from the same provider that makes no assessment (for example UNAVAILABLE) can replace that provider's re-report in the #134 prepass.\n- EV8-1: there are no local receipts for the CLI test files that exercise the changed help text in cli/src/commands/current.js. The help-text grep receipt and the planned hosted CI cover this.\n\nCaveats: I read R1's 'through both entry points' as the entry-point wiring tests plus exhaustive unit tests of the shared checkClaims; unknown-value and unknown-key refusals are tested at the unit level only. Record de-duplication also compares classId, which is a slightly stricter key than AC3 defines, and is harmless. Hosted CI has not run on this head; that is the planned step after convergence."}]}